{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.ChiMinusSix","lean:module:QOU.Information.QouPNeqNp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qou_p_neq_np_of_jetHorizon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qou_p_neq_np_of_jetHorizon","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/JetHorizonTransfer.lean#L63-L73","doc":"**Given a QOU and the jet-horizon transfer, P ≠ NP in the QOU\n(conditional, sorry-free from the hypotheses).**  Composes the\n*derived* non-vanishing `χ(A) = -6 ≠ 0` (`ChiMinusSix.chi_ne_zero`,\nan axiom consequence) with the horizon opacity and the transfer\nbridge.  The entire open content is the `[JetHorizonTransfer]`\ninstance — the degree-graded NP-witness/P-answer identification —\nnever a bare `P ≠ NP`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer.transfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer.transfer","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/JetHorizonTransfer.lean#L61-L61","doc":"**The conjectural bridge**: a blocked degree-0 answer (with\ndegree-≥1 witnesses leaking) yields the QOU decision separation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer.opacity_of_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer.opacity_of_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/JetHorizonTransfer.lean#L58-L58","doc":"A nonzero universal obstruction forces degree-0 horizon opacity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer.degreeZeroBlocked","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer.degreeZeroBlocked","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/JetHorizonTransfer.lean#L56-L56","doc":"`Γ(𝓗, A₀) = 0`: degree-0 sections vanish on the jet horizon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer.mk","kind":"ctor","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/JetHorizonTransfer.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.JetHorizonTransfer","kind":"class","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/JetHorizonTransfer.lean#L39-L61","doc":"**The jet-horizon transfer (§3b-cond conjectural class).**  Encodes\nthe corpus's degree-graded horizon mechanism for a QOU obstruction of\nscalar value `chi`.\n\n* `degreeZeroBlocked` — the proposition `Γ(𝓗, A₀) = 0` (degree-0\n  sections vanish on the horizon: the P-answer is inaccessible);\n* `opacity_of_obstruction` — a nonzero obstruction induces that\n  opacity (`res ≠ 0 ⇒ Γ(𝓗,A₀)=0`);\n* `transfer` — the **conjectural counting→decision bridge**: with\n  the degree-0 answer blocked and degree-≥1 witnesses leaking,\n  `P ≠ NP` holds in the QOU.\n\nNo instance is provided — `transfer` is the open identification. The\n`decisionCost` parameter names the QOU decision-cost family whose\nnon-poly-boundedness (`PNeqNPInQOU decisionCost`) the transfer targets. ","signatureChunk":0}]}